  "description": "II-11 through the ACE OLE DB provider (DAO refuses CREATE VIEW/PROCEDURE with 3290). Over a DAO-built T(ID, A), ADO runs CREATE VIEW V1, CREATE PROCEDURE P1 (select), CREATE PROCEDURE P2 (pId LONG) as an UPDATE, CREATE VIEW V2 ... WITH OWNERACCESS OPTION, then EXEC P2 1 and a SELECT from V1. DAO reopens and lists QueryDefs (Name, Type, SQL, refreshed); ADO then runs DROP VIEW V1 and DROP PROCEDURE P1 and DAO lists again. Asks which saved objects these create, how DAO sees them, and whether the OWNERACCESS clause survives.",
  "callerSurface": "native-idispatch/x64",
  "invokeLcid": 1033,
  "observationRecipe": [
    "clearErrorInfoBefore",
